This C++ function is meant to return the index of target in a sorted vector, or -1. It has two bugs.

```cpp
int find(const std::vector<int>& v, int target) {
    int lo = 0, hi = v.size();
    while (lo < hi) {
        int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;
        if (v[mid] == target) return mid;
        if (v[mid] < target) hi = mid;
        else lo = mid + 1;
    }
    return -1;
}
```

